## Choosing the Right Collection

A library catalog needs all three collections working together:

- **Vec** — to show books in order, like a shelf list
- **Map** — to look up books by ISBN instantly
- **Set** — to track genres without duplicates

### The Data Model

```xiom
let book_list: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
let isbn_lookup: Map[Str,Str] = Map[Str,Str].new();
let genres: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
```

### Adding a Book

```xiom
fn add_book(title: Str, isbn: Str, genre: Str) {
  book_list.push(title);
  isbn_lookup.insert(isbn, title);
  genres.insert(genre);
}
```

Each collection serves a different purpose:
- `book_list` keeps the order books were added
- `isbn_lookup` maps ISBN → title for fast search
- `genres` tracks all unique genres in the library

### Looking Up by ISBN

```xiom
fn find_by_isbn(isbn: Str) {
  match isbn_lookup.get(isbn) {
    Some(title) -> io.println("Found: " + title);
    None -> io.println("No book with that ISBN");
  }
}
```

### Full Program

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let books: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  let catalog: Map[Str,Str] = Map[Str,Str].new();
  let tags: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();

  books.push("The Great Gatsby");
  catalog.insert("978-0743273565", "The Great Gatsby");
  tags.insert("Fiction");

  books.push("A Brief History of Time");
  catalog.insert("978-0553380163", "A Brief History of Time");
  tags.insert("Science");

  io.println("Books: " + string.int_to_str(books.len()));
  io.println("Genres: " + string.int_to_str(tags.len()));

  match catalog.get("978-0743273565") {
    Some(title) -> io.println("Found by ISBN: " + title);
    None -> io.println("Not found");
  }

  return 0;
}
```

